  "note": "Lean keeps the strategy: Cauchy–Schwarz plus Mellin–Plancherel, giving √T₀·log. Erratum: In the proof of Lemma 9.1.4 the Cauchy–Schwarz bound for ∫₁^∞|f′|g_χ is |η·log|₂√((1/π)∫g_χ²), and the summing step uses |η·log|₂√(∫g_χ²); for η = t²e^{−t²/2}, δ = 0, q = 1, T₀ = 10, ∫₁^{T₀}|f′|g_χ = 16.92 > 12.65 and ∫₁^{T₀}|f′|² = 0.194 > |η·log|₂² = 0.1636, while Plancherel gives (1/2π)∫|G′|² = |η·log|₂² (the book omits the square). (checked by `scripts/checks/lemma_9_1_4.py`)."
